IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bca-core`

-- Building Control Act 1989, ss 4, 12, 20, 22A, 25H and 29B -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_bca.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`an extension built without approval` MEANS Works WITH
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS FALSE
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS FALSE
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS FALSE
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS FALSE

`an approved extension built to plan` MEANS Works WITH
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS FALSE
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS TRUE
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS FALSE
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS FALSE

`an approved extension built a storey higher` MEANS Works WITH
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS FALSE
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS TRUE
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS TRUE
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS FALSE

`an approved extension that deviated without the contractor's knowledge` MEANS Works WITH
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS FALSE
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS TRUE
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS TRUE
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS TRUE

`insignificant works without approval` MEANS Works WITH
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS TRUE
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS FALSE
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS FALSE
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS FALSE

